{"name":"Spring","hex":"#00f900","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Spring","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A census-designated place in Harris County, Texas, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Spring"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spring (season)","blocks":[{"text":"Spring, also known as springtime, is one of the four temperate seasons, succeeding winter and preceding summer. There are various technical definitions of spring, but local usage of the term varies according to local climate, cultures and customs. When it is spring in the Northern Hemisphere, it is autumn in the Southern Hemisphere and vice versa. At the spring equinox, also called the vernal equinox, days and nights are approximately twelve hours long, with daytime length increasing and nighttime length decreasing as the season progresses until the summer solstice. The spring equinox is in March in the Northern Hemisphere and in September in the Southern Hemisphere, while the summer solstice is in June in the Northern Hemisphere and in December in the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Arboretum_Robert_Lenoir_-_Jardin_des_m%C3%A9llif%C3%A8res.jpg/330px-Arboretum_Robert_Lenoir_-_Jardin_des_m%C3%A9llif%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_(season)"},{"title":"Spring (device)","blocks":[{"text":"A spring is a device consisting of an elastic but largely rigid material bent or molded into a form that can return into shape after being compressed, extended or twisted. Springs can store energy when compressed, when extended, and/or when twisted. In everyday use, the term most often refers to coil springs, but there are many different spring designs. Modern springs are typically manufactured from spring steel. An example of a non-metallic spring is the bow, made traditionally of flexible yew wood, which when drawn stores energy to propel an arrow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Federkennlinie.svg/330px-Federkennlinie.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_(device)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/500px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/1280px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/500px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cherry blossoms flowering during springtime in Christchurch, New Zealand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg/500px-Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg/1280px-Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn